  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The principal physical and chemical characteristics of interstitial&nbsp;compounds are as follows:</p><p>(i) They have high melting points, higher than those of pure metals.</p><p>(ii) They are very hard, some borides approach diamond in hardness.</p><p>(iii) They retain metallic conductivity.</p><p>(iv) They are chemically inert.</p>",
